  "title": "Computation Operations",
  "emoji": "➕",
  "parentNote": "Use loose coins, buttons, or beads for carrying/borrowing and for multiplication arrays — seeing \"10 ones become 1 ten\" with real objects makes it click.",
  "learnBullets": [
    "**Addition** with carrying (regrouping) — 2 and 3-digit numbers",
    "**Subtraction** with borrowing (regrouping)",
    "**Multiplication** as repeated addition (tables up to 5)",
    "**Division** as equal sharing",
    "Simple word problems using all four operations"
  ],
  "learnItFirst": "**Addition with carrying:**\n```\n   38\n + 47\n ----\n  8 + 7 = 15 → write 5, carry 1\n  3 + 4 + 1(carried) = 8\n ----\n   85\n```\n\n**Subtraction with borrowing:**\n```\n   82\n - 35\n ----\n  2 is smaller than 5, so borrow 1 ten: 12 − 5 = 7\n  Now tens: 7 − 3 = 4\n ----\n   47\n```\n\n**Multiplication** = repeated addition:\n```\n4 × 3  =  4 + 4 + 4  =  12\n```\n\n**Division** = equal sharing:\n```\n12 ÷ 3  →  share 12 into 3 equal groups  →  4 in each group\n```\n\n### 🧠 How to Solve — 3 Easy Steps\n1. **Line up** the ones, tens, and hundreds columns carefully.\n2. **Start from the ones column** — carry or borrow if needed.\n3. For word problems: **decide the operation** first (add, subtract, multiply, or divide) before calculating.\n\n---",
